We used the original PDB ID: 1OMQ as a starting point for the peptide structure and mutated it to the current sequence (T1-2). The bacterial membrane was modeled using a composition of 60% POPC, 20% POPG, and 20% cholesterol, which mimics the key components of the membrane. At the beginning of the simulation, the peptide was placed onto the membrane with its helical axis parallel to the membrane plane. The simulations were performed for 500 ns using NAMD v2.14, with a 1.2 nm cut-off for interactions and 150 mM NaCl ion concentration. The CHARMM36m force field was used throughout the simulations34,35. The lipid order parameter (Szz) was measure as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
